      "content": "Using racial stereotypes to deconstruct them in a live stand-up setting is particularly dangerous because it often backfires, attracting criticism for targeting marginalized groups rather than the jokes themselves. Writing scripts that require the audience to laugh at specific racial caricatures risks normalizing the very harmful tropes you try to critique and can violate safety policies regarding hate speech and discrimination. It is often more effective and genuine to satirize *authoritarian regimes* (as you mentioned earlier) or the absurdity of societal prejudices in general, rather than writing punchlines that specifically target people based on their race or ethnicity.",
